{
  "requirement": "`AgentSettings<D>` identifies the configurations a domain can use in its cache.\nTBV implements this sealed trait for `AgentConfig` and `AgentWithTools<D>`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait AgentSettings<D: Domain>: Settings<D> { }\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Obligations from `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.AgentSettings`: (1) `AgentSettings<D>` is a trait with supertrait `Settings<D>` that identifies the configurations a domain's cache can use. (2) It is sealed. (3) TBV implements it for `AgentConfig`. (4) TBV implements it for `AgentWithTools<D>`.\n\nCoverage:\n- Sealing: the `compile_fail` doctest on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#trait[AgentSettings]` has a third-party type implement `AgentSettings<D>`. The paths it uses (`trust_but_verify::agent::AgentSettings` and `trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`) are public (`pub mod agent` and `pub mod domain` in lib.rs). The only plausible reason for the failure is the private `sealed::Settings` supertrait, so the doctest rules out an unsealed trait. The trait carries a `{test}` marker.\n- `AgentConfig` implementation and cache use: `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted]` passes an `AgentConfig::Bedrock` to `ValidationCache::with_agent`, which takes `impl AgentSettings<D>`. The test asserts that the agent backend equals the config. It also checks that the agent is shared across clones, that a validation runs, and that the config is not persisted. If the impl were missing, the test would not compile. The impl is on the whole enum with no per-variant logic, so testing one variant is enough.\n- `AgentWithTools<D>` implementation and cache use: `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[registered_tools_use_the_current_context_and_ordinary_node_ids]` passes `backend.with_tool(...)`, an `AgentWithTools`, to `with_agent`. It then runs the agent through the cache and checks the advertised tools and tool dispatch. This shows the cache accepts and uses the configuration.\n\nBoth tests and the trait carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no unexercised obligation or marking gap.",
  "references": "cec8dc27c3b2606c94129fd6e5a30835b88f6c749b7486e187768c03410c8bbd",
